### 1. Bug Scenario Images & Reasoning

**Image 1:**  
Shows the HTML source code with `<link rel="preconnect" ...>` for both `https://www.google-analytics.com` and `https://fonts.gstatic.com`.

**Image 2:**  
Lighthouse audit still suggests adding preconnect/dns-prefetch for `https://www.google-analytics.com` and `https://fonts.googleapis.com`, even though preconnect is already present for the relevant origins.

**Root Cause:**  
The audit logic in `lighthouse-core/audits/uses-rel-preconnect.js` does not check the DOM for existing `<link rel="preconnect">` or `<link rel="dns-prefetch">` tags. As a result, it recommends preconnect even when it is already implemented.

---

### 2. Bug Code Snippet Analysis

The code in `lighthouse-core/audits/uses-rel-preconnect.js` only analyzes network records and does not check the DOM for existing preconnect/dns-prefetch links.  
**To fix:**  
- The audit should also check the DOM for `<link rel="preconnect">` and `<link rel="dns-prefetch">` and exclude those origins from the recommendations.

---

### 3. Patch Generation

We need to:
- Add `LinkElements` to `requiredArtifacts`.
- Fetch `LinkElements` in the audit.
- Filter out origins that already have a preconnect/dns-prefetch link.

